# Paths exempt from scripts/scan-credentials.py, with the reason.
#
# An exemption in code is an exemption nobody reviews, so they live here as
# data: every one shows up in a diff and has to be justified in the pull
# request that adds it.
#
# Format:  path/to/file  # why
#
# These three exist to prove that redaction works. Each plants a token or a
# password and asserts it does not survive into a report or a log. Remove the
# planted value and the test can no longer fail, which would leave the real
# redaction path unguarded -- a strictly worse outcome than the exemption.
scripts/regression/verify-curl-authorization-stripped.py   # planted password; asserts curl export strips Authorization
scripts/regression/verify-reporter-redaction.js            # planted JWT; asserts the reporter redacts bearer tokens
scripts/regression/verify-result-emitter-redaction.py      # planted JWT; asserts the result emitter redacts AUTH_TOKEN
